al with an aperture more than 13 mm, but less than 100 mm.\\\\r\\\\n21,404\\\\r\\\\nClause 3.9.3.2\\\\r\\\\nSUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\",\\\"section\\\":null,\\\"score\\\":1,\\\"originalUrl\\\":\\\"/api/standards-library?document=82243ecea0760d56368c3ee94741bf47c53ca7eb37a37e4e09dfbc69f5aaad78#page=350\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"library:768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823:350\\\",\\\"documentId\\\":\\\"768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823\\\",\\\"documentName\\\":\\\"BCA_96_Volume_Two_Amdt_01_0.pdf\\\",\\\"edition\\\":\\\"Edition not established\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823\\\",\\\"page\\\":350,\\\"text\\\":\\\"21,404 PART \\\\r\\\\n⎯\\\\r\\\\n3.9.3.2 \\\\r\\\\n3.9.3.3 \\\\r\\\\nNote: l . \\\\r\\\\n3.9 - SAFE MOVEMENT AND ACCESS \\\\r\\\\nBuilding Code of Australia 1996 Volume Two \\\\r\\\\nFigure \\\\r\\\\nSPACING OF ACCESSIBLE HORIZONTAL MEMBERS, PROJECTIONS OR \\\\r\\\\nINDENTATIONS IN FENCING \\\\r\\\\nFigure \\\\r\\\\nCHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE \\\\r\\\\nFencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but ess than 100 mm\\\\r\\\\nClause 3.9.3.2 \\\\r\\\\nSUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\",\\\"section\\\":null,\\\"score\\\":1,\\\"originalUrl\\\":\\\"/api/standards-library?document=768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823#page=350\\\"}],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"## Chain wire fencing mesh aperture - Australian Standard research\\n\\n### Important clarification first\\nNo active tool in the X-Ray app supports live web search. I cannot reach the current public web to retrieve a publisher page for the question. I have only the **local Standards library** available, and below is what that source actually returns.\\n\\n### What the local library returned (the only evidence I can cite)\\nA search for \\\"chain wire fencing mesh aperture\\\" returned **only excerpts from the Building Code of Australia (BCA) Volume Two, Part 3.9 \\\"Safe movement and access\\\"**, across multiple superseded editions (1996 amendments, 2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009). The relevant text in every hit is the same:\\n\\n- \\\"Figure 3.9.3.3 CHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE — Fencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but less than 100 mm.\\\"\\n- Source: \\\"Clause 3.9.3.3 Australian Building Codes Board\\\" — and each excerpt carries the stamp \\\"SUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\".\\n\\nThis **defines an aperture range**, not a mesh-aperture spec for chain-wire, and it is **not the primary product/aperture standard** for chain-wire fencing mesh.\\n\\n### What the local library did **not** return\\n- No current, non-superseded edition of BCA Vol 2 covering this clause.\\n- No excerpt from an Australian Standard such as **AS 1725** (Chain link fence / Chain link security fencing) or its successor.\\n- No edition label or cited year for an AS aperture clause — only BCA stamp.\\n\\n### So I will **not** give you \\\"AS 1725-2014\\\" or similar\\n- I have no retrieved web or library excerpt that confirms a designation, year or publisher URL for the Australian Standard governing chain-wire mesh aperture.\\n- Citing one would be an invented reference, and my rules forbid that.\\n\\n### What would actually answer your question\\nA live web fetch via an external browser is not available from inside this assistant. The reliable citation must come from Standards Australia directly (e.g. `https://www.standards.org.au`), referencing the current edition of **AS 1725** (Chain link security fencing and gates) for product/aperture requirements, with BCA Vol 2 / NCC Vol 2 covering the \\\"safe movement and access\\\" use conditions.\\n\\n### Sources I actually retrieved\\n| # | Document (local library) | Edition label returned | Page | Snippet |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | BCA 96 Vol 2 Amdt 11 | Edition not established | 337 | \\\"Fencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but less than 100 mm.\\\" (superseded) |\\n| 2 | BCA 96 Vol 2 Amdt 12 | Edition not established | 356 | Same note, superseded |\\n| 3 | BCA 2004 Vol 2 | 2004 | 380 | Same note, superseded |\\n| 4 | BCA 2007 Vol 2 | 2007 | 394 | Same note, superseded |\\n| 5 | BCA 2009 Vol 2 | 2009 | 403 | Same note, superseded |\\n\\nRetrieved via `search_standards_library` on `2025-01-25` against the local NCC/BCA reference PDFs.\\n\\n### Honest answer\\n- **Exact AS designation:** not retrieved — local library returned only superseded BCA excerpts, and web search is not available from this tool surface.\\n- **Year of publication:** not verified by any retrieved excerpt.\\n- **Official source URL:** none fetched.\\n\\nRecommend re-running this question from a session with web access pointed at Standards Australia for AS 1725 and the current NCC Vol 2 to confirm the live edition and clauses.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Developer review\\n- **Outcome:** Reported an inability to cite a current Australian Standard precisely, and surfaced what the local library actually holds, instead of inventing a designation, year or URL.\\n- **Friction:** User asked for \\\"current web\\\" results, but no live web tool is exposed; this was a hard environment limit, not a reasoning gap, and the answer would have benefited from saying so earlier in the headline.\\n- **Improvement:** Lead the reply with the one-line \\\"web search is not available here; only a local BCA Vol 2 excerpt was retrieved\\\" so the user sees the limitation before the evidence list.\"}],\"projectId\":\"job-da2d2767-cea0-4c2d-8b4d-3d9d5f349256\",\"activeId\":\"2d48c8e6-935d-4e8d-9be2-4cc7141e4e9e\",\"threads\":2,\"busy\":false,\"error\":null,\"workPacket\":{\"state\":\"review-required\",\"objective\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\",\"nextAction\":\"Workflow receipts complete. Review the draft against its sources and acceptance tests; no professional approval or issue recorded.\",\"pendingAction\":null,\"routingFailure\":null},\"entries\":[{\"kind\":\"user\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_workflow_route\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"version\\\":\\\"xray.workflow/1\\\",\\\"workflow\\\":\\\"discussion\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[\\\"Discuss capabilities or plans; do not claim project actions occurred.\\\"],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Workflow selection only; no geometry, evidence or authority changed.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"search_standards_library\",\"failed\":true,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-executed\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Workflow prerequisite missing.\\\",\\\"requestedTool\\\":\\\"search_standards_library\\\",\\\"next\\\":{\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read_project_context\\\",\\\"args\\\":{},\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Read the current project identity, revision and workspace state.\\\"}}\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_project_context\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"projectId\\\":\\\"job-da2d2767-cea0-4c2d-8b4d-3d9d5f349256\\\",\\\"projectName\\\":\\\"New project\\\",\\\"projectRevision\\\":1,\\\"pane\\\":\\\"cost\\\",\\\"sourcePage